Supplementary Table 14: Pathways and protein complexes prioritized by DEPICT. The Data-driven Enrichment-Prioritized Integration for Complex Traits (DEPICT) method re-annotates gene sets based on large-scale gene expression data and then identifie reconstituted gene sets that enrich for genes within associated loci. Locus gene sets were constructed by mapping genes to a given locus if they were within, or overlapped with, regions defined by linkage disequilibrium r2>0.5 around the lead SNP of the given locus. The table lists 301 gene sets with P<1x10-11). The ‘Reconstituted gene set ID’ column lists the gene set ID of the original gene set. Reconstituted gene sets starting with GO are derived from the Gene Ontology database; gene sets starting with MP are derived phenotypic gene sets from the Mouse Genome Informatics database; gene sets starting with ENSG are derived protein-protein interaction subnetworks from the InWeb database; and prefixes KEGG and REACTOME refer to gene sets derived from the KEGG and REACTOME databases, respectively). Gene sets were pruned into meta gene sets based on fraction of shared genes (Jaccard index > 0.25). The column ‘Part of meta gene set’ lists the meta gene set a given gene set may be part of. 	Unnamed: 1	Unnamed: 2	Unnamed: 3	Unnamed: 4	Unnamed: 5
